{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1782344292,"nonce":"iviFoY8NdZSSYp06PQvAJ//gz3s=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lAHOK4fCvM8AAAABGnuD687IQByf"},"target":"e8297eaf640eca49ff927d620db7beed0d54e74801cb2f2bf4b3aceb1e6294d5","message":"## Problem\n\nThe `global_costmap` inflation layer for bizzy still carries **BEN's tuning** —\n`inflation_radius: 150.0`, `cost_scaling_factor: 0.05` — inherited from\n`ben_project11/nav2_params.yaml` via `echoboat_project11/config/nav2_params.base.yaml`.\nBEN is a larger ASV and the 150 m inflation was an intentional coastline/obstacle\nstandoff. When the echoboat **local** costmap was retuned (`inflation_radius: 3.0`,\n`cost_scaling_factor: 1.0`) the **global** costmap was left at BEN's values.\n\nThis was harmless on bizzy while it had **no global depth prior** (s57 `chart_layer`\ndisabled for bizzy 2026-06-12). Wiring the **`bathymetry_layer`** into the bizzy global\ncostmap (#319/#322) is the first thing to place hard-lethal cells across that costmap —\nall land + every unsurveyed/gap cell via `unsurveyed_is_lethal: true`. The 150 m\ninflation then expands that lethal margin into the navigable water.\n\n## Evidence (headless bizzy sim, 2026-06-24)\n\nRan `ros2 launch marine_simulation sim_robot_launch.py platform:=bizzy`. The\n`bathymetry_layer` itself integrates correctly (loads in both costmaps, `~`-expands the\nstore path, tide gate opens at z=48.881 m, query level 10 matches the imported tiles,\nprojection + per-cell clearance costs are sane — boat ≈ navigable ramp, open water ≈\nnear-free). **But the composite `global_costmap` reads ~100 % LETHAL including the\nboat's own surveyed position**; only ~470 cells are navigable. Proof it is inflation,\nnot bathymetry clearance: at the open-water patch the bathymetry layer's own cost is ≈3\n(near-free) yet the composite is 240/245; at the boat the layer's own cost is ≈225\n(navigable) yet the composite is 254. The `sea_surface_relay` grid was empty. Lake\nMassabesic's surveyed corridors are often \u003c 300 m wide, so a 150 m standoff from both\nshores (+ the lethal land ring) closes them — the planner cannot operate.\n\n## Fix (this issue)\n\nOverride the **bizzy** global costmap inflation to match the local costmap\n(`cost_scaling_factor: 1.0`, `inflation_radius: 3.0`) in\n`bizzyboat_project11/config/nav2_overlay.yaml`. Scoped to the bizzy overlay (not the\nshared base) so the seafloor echoboat — which still uses `chart_layer` + `obstacle_layer`\nin open water, where BEN's 150 m standoff may be intended — is unaffected. The\nbathymetry **clearance ramp** already provides depth-based shore-keepoff (shallow = high\ncost), so a large geometric inflation is redundant for shore avoidance.\n\nVerify in the headless sim that the lake opens up (navigable interior, boat free,\nshore/land still lethal) after the change.\n\n## Follow-ups (not this issue)\n\n- Revisit whether `unsurveyed_is_lethal: true` should soften to high-cost-not-lethal.\n- Decide if the global inflation retune should eventually move to the echoboat base\n  (would also affect izzy / seafloor echoboat — needs their own evaluation).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1782348267,"nonce":"TTWiUSRd2KOXk3NcIcTTp9RD1UU=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABHct9Eg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/327#issuecomment-4794842386"},"message":"Sim correction: the headless re-run with inflation at 3 m showed the global costmap is **still ~100 % lethal** — so this inflation retune is correct cleanup but is **not** the navigability fix. The lake-wide lethal flood is a `bathymetry_layer` window-anchor bug, tracked in rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#220. PR #328 implements this issue's inflation change on its own merits.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M 